    #     resolved from git by its subject, and the record commit made after
    #     part 4a's push (335da53, subject "M2 part 4a close-out record") is
    #     checked to be in the range exactly once. The usage names
    #     m2p4bclose-push.sh. The script, its library copy and each attempt's
    #     output are kept under <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p4b-close/.
    #     Change 8 stands unchanged.
    #
    # Milestone 2 part 4a close-out push.log
    # (specs/0019-names-links-properties-protection.md, "Close-out push (after
    # P4)", and "Planning verification and rulings on P4 (2026-09-28)", ruling 15).
    #
    # CARRIED TO M2 part 4a from part 3's close-out push script (printed in
    # records/logs/m2p3-close/push.log, whose own change list follows). Every
    # check, control and helper is that text's, unchanged, except:
    #  7. The names are M2 part 4a's, the spec cited is specs/0019, the base is
    #     part 3's close-out doc commit (6dbb4a0 when this was written), resolved
    #     from git by its subject, and the record commit made after part 3's push
    #     (5e57db1, subject "M2 part 3 close-out record") is checked to be in the
    #     range exactly once. The usage names m2p4aclose-push.sh. The script, its
    #     library copy and each attempt's output are kept under
    #     <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p4a-close/.
    #  8. Planning's close-out word: push.log records the maintainer's typed
    #     authorisation verbatim and its date. push mode reads them from the
    #     inputs MAINTAINER_AUTH and MAINTAINER_AUTH_DATE, prints both on
    #     labelled input lines and in one sentence, and refuses to push when
    #     either is empty.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M2 part 3 from part 2's close-out push script (printed in
    # records/logs/m2p2-close/push.log, whose own change list follows). Every
    # check, control and helper is that text's, unchanged, except:
    #  5. The names are M2 part 3's, the spec cited is specs/0018, the base is
    #     part 2's close-out doc commit (42588cc when this was written), resolved
    #     from git by its subject, and the record commit made after part 2's push
    #     (d0f8f72, subject "M2 part 2 close-out record") is checked to be in the
    #     range exactly once. The usage names m2p3close-push.sh.
    #  6. specs/0018 P4 ruling 7: this script, its counting library copy and each
    #     attempt's output are also kept on disk under
    #     <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p3-close/ by the caller; the scratch copy is
    #     the one that runs.
    #
    # CARRIED FROM M2 part 1's close-out push script (printed in
    # records/logs/m2p1-close/push.log). Every check, control and helper is that
    # text's, unchanged, except:
    #  1. The names are M2 part 2's, and the spec cited is specs/0017.
    #  2. The base is part 1's close-out doc commit (c115d45 when this was
    #     written), the last commit part 1 pushed, resolved from git by its
    #     subject and the pattern asserted to match exactly one commit. Part 1's
    #     close-out record commit, made after its push, is in this range; a check
    #     says so.
    #  3. P1 verification ruling 7 of specs/0017: the script's standard error
    #     goes to a file under <scratch> from its start, and each mode's last
    #     block counts it expecting 0, with a control on a copy one byte longer.
    #  4. Part 1's header items stand: the self-scan before the script prints
    #     itself and again at the start of push mode, the identity section, the
    #     blob scan, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY unset as a check, the denylist counted and
    #     never printed, the path check on each mode's captured output, nine gate
    #     steps, one record commit after the push.
    #
    # Usage: M1CLOSE_LIB=<lib> m7p1close-push.sh pre <phase commit> > <scratch file>
    #          step 2: the environment, identity, blob-scan, hook, core.hooksPath
    #          and denylist checks and the full gate; records the base
    #          (origin/main) and the count of commits to push. NO PUSH, and this
    #          mode can never push.
    #        M1CLOSE_LIB=<lib> m7p1close-push.sh identity <base> <tip>
    #          the identity section alone over base..tip. NO PUSH.
    #        M1CLOSE_LIB=<lib> m7p1close-push.sh push <base> >> <scratch file>
    #          steps 3 and 4: refuses unless origin/main still equals <base>,
    #          pushes, and checks the hook's range, the count and git's report
    #          against <base> as recorded by pre, never against origin/main read
    #          after the push.
    #
    # THE MAINTAINER'S AUTHORISATION. specs/0003-ci.md, the section on the push,
    # requires three preconditions: the phase DONE, planning's word, and the
    # maintainer typing authorisation in the implementing session. push mode is
    # only ever run after that sentence has been typed. Planning's word does not
    # stand in for it, and neither does this script.
    #
    # Every commit id this log reports is read from git at run time by a command
    # the log prints; none is typed.
    set -uo pipefail
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    
    MODE=${1:?pre or push}
    # Change 3: this script's own standard error, per mode, counted at the end.
    ERR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)/out/push-$MODE.stderr
    mkdir -p "$(dirname "$ERR")" || exit 2
    exec 2>"$ERR"
    # err_block: the stderr count and its control, printed in each mode's last
    # block.
    err_block() {
      local nerr nerr_ctl
      nerr=$(wc -c <"$ERR")
      cp "$ERR" "$T/c-err"; printf 'x' >>"$T/c-err"
      nerr_ctl=$(wc -c <"$T/c-err")
      echo "## this script's own standard error (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
      echo "  command: wc -c <scratch>/close/out/push-$MODE.stderr: $nerr bytes; a copy with one byte appended: $nerr_ctl"
      check "this script wrote nothing to its standard error" "$(yn [ "$nerr" = 0 ])"
      check "control: the same count reads one byte more in the copy" "$(yn [ "$nerr_ctl" = "$((nerr + 1))" ])"
    }
    LIB=${M1CLOSE_LIB:?the path to the counting library is required}
    . "$LIB"
    REPO=thekeoni1/emend
    URL=https://github.com/thekeoni1/emend.git
    BASE_PATTERN='^M6 part 6 close-out: commit planning docs [(]the P4 verification and rulings[)]$'
    TIP_SUBJECT='M7 part 1 close-out: commit planning docs (the P2 verification and rulings)'
    PREV_RECORD_PATTERN='^M6 part 6 close-out record'
    ID_FILE=scripts/privacy-identity.txt
    DENY_FILE=$HOME/.config/emend/private-denylist.txt
    export GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never
    # Change 31 (specs/0032 P3 verification ruling 4): temporary files live
    # under the close-out's phase directory, the parent of this script's own,
    # never the system temporary directory; every tool run here inherits it.
    TMPDIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)/tmp
    export TMPDIR
    mkdir -p "$TMPDIR" || exit 2
    T=$(mktemp -d)
    trap 'rm -rf "${T:?}"' EXIT
    # Change 35 (specs/0033 "Planning rulings on P1", ruling 12): the one
    # mktemp directory is checked to lie under TMPDIR, with a control; this
    # script makes no plain mktemp file. under_dir <path> <dir>: the path
    # lies strictly below the directory.
    under_dir() { case "$1" in "$2"/?*) return 0 ;; *) return 1 ;; esac; }
    # mk_counts_ok: one mktemp call, a directory, and no plain file.
    mk_counts_ok() { [ "$N_MK" = 1 ] && [ "$N_MKF" = 0 ]; }
    SCRATCH_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
    fail=0
    
    show() { echo "$1:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$2"; }
    check() { echo "$1: $2"; [ "$2" = yes ] || fail=1; }
    yn() { if "$@"; then echo yes; else echo no; fi; }
    # exit_and_bytes <exit> <bytes> <want exit> <want bytes>: both match, in one
    # function so neither condition is dropped.
    exit_and_bytes() { [ "$1" -eq "$3" ] && [ "$2" = "$4" ]; }
    # same_nonempty <a> <b>: both set and equal.
    same_nonempty() { [ -n "$1" ] && [ "$1" = "$2" ]; }
    # holds_once <file> <line>: the file holds that whole line exactly once.
    holds_once() { [ "$(count_matches -F "$2" "$1")" = 1 ]; }
    # tree_clean: git status ran and printed nothing.
    tree_clean() { [ "$(run_lines git status --porcelain)" = 0 ]; }
    # show_status: the status lines themselves and their count (P2 verification
    # ruling 2, F1).
    show_status() {
      echo "command: git status --porcelain -> $(run_lines git status --porcelain) line(s)"
      git status --porcelain 2>&1 | sed 's/^/    /'
    }
    # files_listed <n>: the range's file list was read and is not empty.
    files_listed() { [ "$1" != error ] && [ "$1" -gt 0 ]; }
    # hook_scanned <file> <commits>: the hook's summary names that many commits and
    # zero findings.
    hook_scanned() {
      [ "$(count_matches -E "^privacy: $2 commit[(]s[)], [0-9]+ blob[(]s[)] scanned, 0 finding[(]s[)]$" "$1")" = 1 ]
    }
    # The phase commit guard (specs/0001, M1 part 3 P1 ruling 11): a full 40-hex
    # sha equal to HEAD. /usr/bin/grep explicitly, as every scan form.
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    full_sha() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C /usr/bin/grep -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; }
    is_head() { full_sha "$1" && [ "$1" = "$HEAD_SHA" ]; }
    not_head() { if is_head "$1"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    # one_line <n>: a count that was read and is exactly 1.
    # id_usable <name> <email>: both set, the email with an @.
    id_usable() { [ -n "$1" ] && [ -n "$2" ] && [ "${2#*@}" != "$2" ]; }
    # ident_read_ok <exit> <commits read> <commits in range>: git log exited 0 and
    # read one line per commit.
    ident_read_ok() { [ "$1" -eq 0 ] && [ "$2" = "$3" ]; }
    # ident_controls_ok <ok> <bad author email> <bad committer name>: the identity
    # counts 0 and each planted mismatch counts 1.
    ident_controls_ok() { [ "$1" = 0 ] && [ "$2" = 1 ] && [ "$3" = 1 ]; }
    # ident_lines <range> <out>: one line per commit, "<an>|<ae>|<cn>|<ce>".
    ident_lines() { git log --format='%an|%ae|%cn|%ce' "$1" >"$2" 2>/dev/null; }
    # ident_mismatches <file> <name> <email>: lines not equal to the identity in all
    # four fields; prints a count, never a field.
    ident_mismatches() {
      awk -F'|' -v n="$2" -v e="$3" 'NF != 4 || $1 != n || $2 != e || $3 != n || $4 != e { c++ } END { print c + 0 }' "$1"
    }
    one_line() { [ "$1" != error ] && [ "$1" = 1 ]; }
    # The path form (header change 6): lines naming a home, mount, temp or corpus
    # path. no_paths <files...>: the form read every file and found none.
    PATH_RE='(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|/tmp/|emend-testing)'
    no_paths() { [ "$(count_matches -E "$PATH_RE" "$@")" = 0 ]; }
    # path_control: a planted path, assembled at run time so this script's own text
    # carries none, must count 1 through the same form, and a clean line 0. It
    # prints its two counts and sets path_ctl_ok; it is not run inside yn, so its
    # printed line is not swallowed.
    path_control() {
      printf 'x %s%s%s y\n' '/ho' 'me/someone/' 'emend-testing/corpus/x.xlsx' >"$T/path-plant"
      printf 'x clean y\n' >"$T/path-clean"
      local a b
      a=$(count_matches -E "$PATH_RE" "$T/path-plant")
      b=$(count_matches -E "$PATH_RE" "$T/path-clean")
      echo "  control: the path form on a planted path: $a (expect 1); on a clean line: $b (expect 0)"
      path_ctl_ok=no
      if [ "$a" = 1 ] && [ "$b" = 0 ]; then path_ctl_ok=yes; fi
    }
    # denylist_usable <n>: the denylist was read and has entries.
    denylist_usable() { [ "$1" != error ] && [ "$1" -gt 0 ]; }
    # The self-scan (specs/0001, "Rules for every phase", the push and ci-run
    # bullet; specs/0015 close-out ruling 5): the three shape greps over this
    # script as it is about to run, before it prints itself, each with a control
    # through the same command form. The patterns and the fixture are assembled
    # from pieces at run time, so this script's own text holds none of them.
    D='$'
    SHAPE_CHAIN="\\${D}\\((yn|is|isnot) .*(&&|\\|\\|)"
    SHAPE_BANG="\\${D}\\((yn|is|isnot) !"
    SHAPE_ASSIGN="\\${D}\\((yn|is|isnot) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*="
    self_shapes() {
      local shape var n_self n_fix
      echo "## the three shape greps, over this script as it is about to run, before it prints itself (specs/0001; specs/0015 close-out ruling 5)"
      printf '%s\n' "x=${D}(is [ 1 ] && true)" "y=${D}(isnot ! true)" "z=${D}(yn N=1 true)" >"$T/shape-fixture"
      echo "command: count_matches -E <shape> <this script>, and the same over a fixture holding one line of each shape"
      for shape in CHAIN BANG ASSIGN; do
        var=SHAPE_$shape
        n_self=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$0")
        n_fix=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$T/shape-fixture")
        echo "  shape $shape: in this script $n_self; in the fixture $n_fix"
        check "$shape: this script holds none" "$(yn [ "$n_self" = 0 ])"
        check "control: $shape: the same form finds the fixture's one line" "$(yn [ "$n_fix" = 1 ])"
      done
    }
    
    # identity_section <base> <main> <count>: the author and committer identity of
    # every commit in base..main against the identity file, counted and never
    # printed, with its controls (change 6).
    identity_section() {
        local BASE=$1 MAIN=$2 COUNT=$3 IDN IDE rc NI MI a b c
        echo
        echo "## the author and committer identity of every commit in the range"
        echo "command: git log --format='%an|%ae|%cn|%ce' $BASE..$MAIN, compared with $ID_FILE lines 1 and 2; no field printed"
        IDN=$(sed -n 1p "$ID_FILE"); IDE=$(sed -n 2p "$ID_FILE")
        check "$ID_FILE holds a name and an email-shaped line 2" "$(yn id_usable "$IDN" "$IDE")"
        ident_lines "$BASE..$MAIN" "$T/ids"; rc=$?
        NI=$(count_lines "$T/ids")
        MI=$(ident_mismatches "$T/ids" "$IDN" "$IDE")
        echo "  exit $rc; commits read: $NI; commits whose author or committer name or email differs: $MI"
        check "one identity line per commit in the range ($NI of $COUNT)" "$(yn ident_read_ok "$rc" "$NI" "$COUNT")"
        check "every commit's author and committer equal the identity file (mismatches $MI)" "$(yn [ "$MI" = 0 ])"
        printf '%s|%s|%s|%s\n' "$IDN" "$IDE" "$IDN" "$IDE" >"$T/id-ok"
        printf '%s|%s|%s|%s\n' "$IDN" "x$IDE" "$IDN" "$IDE" >"$T/id-bad-ae"
        printf '%s|%s|%s|%s\n' "$IDN" "$IDE" "x$IDN" "$IDE" >"$T/id-bad-cn"
        a=$(ident_mismatches "$T/id-ok" "$IDN" "$IDE"); b=$(ident_mismatches "$T/id-bad-ae" "$IDN" "$IDE"); c=$(ident_mismatches "$T/id-bad-cn" "$IDN" "$IDE")
        echo "  control: the same form on the identity itself: $a (expect 0); a planted author-email mismatch: $b (expect 1); a planted committer-name mismatch: $c (expect 1)"
        check "control: the identity form counts a planted mismatch in each case" "$(yn ident_controls_ok "$a" "$b" "$c")"
    }
    # target_dir_ok <value>: the value is this close-out's target root (change 22).
    target_dir_ok() { [ -n "$1" ] && [ "$1" = "$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m7p1-close/target" ]; }
    # excel_record_ok <scratch dir>: at HEAD exactly one file matches
    # records/excel-check-m7-*.md, and it holds a "## Results" heading and at
    # least one table row whose result cell begins with pass, repair or fail
    # (change 65; specs/0044 "The restored Excel-record check" and ruling U).
    # It writes the tree, the matching names, the blob and the count of such
    # cells into the scratch directory and prints nothing.
    excel_record_ok() {
      local d=${1:?a scratch directory} f n
      printf '0\n' >"$d/xr-count"
      git ls-tree -r --name-only HEAD -- records/ >"$d/xr-tree" || return 1
      LC_ALL=C /usr/bin/grep -E '^records/excel-check-m7-[^/]*[.]md$' "$d/xr-tree" >"$d/xr-files"
      [ "$(wc -l <"$d/xr-files")" -eq 1 ] || return 1
      f=$(cat "$d/xr-files")
      git show "HEAD:$f" >"$d/xr-blob" || return 1
      n=$(awk -F'|' '
        $0 == "## Results" { r = 1; next }
        r && /^## / { r = 0 }
        r && /^[|]/ {
          h = 0
          for (i = 2; i < NF; i++) { c = $i; gsub(/^ +| +$/, "", c); if (c == "result") { col = i; h = 1 } }
          if (h || !col) next
          c = $col; gsub(/^ +| +$/, "", c)
          if (c ~ /^(pass|repair|fail)( |$)/) k++
        }
        END { print k + 0 }' "$d/xr-blob")
      printf '%s\n' "$n" >"$d/xr-count"
      [ "$n" -ge 1 ]
    }
    # The same check's negation, for its control.
    excel_record_refused() { if excel_record_ok "$1"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    # excel_record_refused_in <clone> <scratch dir>: the negation, run in a clone.
    excel_record_refused_in() { ( cd "$1" && excel_record_refused "$2" ); }
    case "$MODE" in
      pre)
        C=${2:?the phase commit is required}
        HEAD_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
        echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
        echo "about: M7 part 1 close-out push of main at $(git rev-parse main); HEAD at run: $HEAD_SHA"
        echo "  the phase commit given to this script: $C"
        echo "  git rev-parse HEAD at this run:        $HEAD_SHA"
        check "the phase commit given to this script is HEAD" "$(yn is_head "$C")"
        check "control: the same form refuses a commit that is not HEAD" "$(yn not_head "$NULL_SHA")"
        check "control: the same form refuses a short sha of the real commit" "$(yn not_head "$(printf '%s' "$C" | cut -c1-7)")"
        echo "phase: Milestone 7 part 1 close-out (specs/0044-excel-check.md, \"Close-out push (after P2)\", planning's close-out instruction) push.log, step 2; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
        echo "root: <scratch> stands for the close-out's phase directory in the build cache (change 30); <scratch>/close holds this script, the counting library copy it sources and, in <scratch>/close/out, its own standard error"
        echo "root: <home> stands for the home directory of the account that ran this script"
        if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"; fi
        KSET=$([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY+set}" ] && echo yes || echo no)
        check "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is unset in this shell (set: $KSET)" "$(yn [ "$KSET" = no ])"
        CTD=${CARGO_TARGET_DIR-}
        CTD_SHOW=${CTD:-unset}
        echo "input (environment) CARGO_TARGET_DIR: ${CTD_SHOW/#$HOME\//<home>/}"
        check "CARGO_TARGET_DIR is set and names <home>/.cache/emend-build/m7p1-close/target (change 22; change 64)" "$(yn target_dir_ok "$CTD")"
        check "control: the same check refuses an unset value" "$(yn [ "$(yn target_dir_ok "")" = no ])"
        check "control: the same check refuses another path" "$(yn [ "$(yn target_dir_ok "$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m6p6-close/target")" = no ])"
        echo "input: TMPDIR=<scratch>/tmp (set by this script, made if missing and exported before its one mktemp; change 31; change 35)"
        check "TMPDIR is <scratch>/tmp, under the close-out's phase directory (change 35)" "$(yn [ "$TMPDIR" = "$SCRATCH_DIR/tmp" ])"
        check "this script's mktemp directory lies under TMPDIR (change 35; specs/0033 Planning rulings on P1, ruling 12)" "$(yn under_dir "$T" "$TMPDIR")"
        check "control: the same check refuses a directory beside TMPDIR, not under it (change 35)" "$(yn [ "$(yn under_dir "$TMPDIR-beside/x" "$TMPDIR")" = no ])"
        check "control: the same check refuses TMPDIR itself (change 35)" "$(yn [ "$(yn under_dir "$TMPDIR" "$TMPDIR")" = no ])"
        N_MK=$(/usr/bin/grep -cE '=[$][(]mktemp( -d)?[)]' "$0"); N_MKF=$(/usr/bin/grep -cE '=[$][(]mktemp[)]' "$0")
        printf 'X=%s(mktemp)\n' '$' >"$T/mk-fixture"; N_MKC=$(/usr/bin/grep -cE '=[$][(]mktemp[)]' "$T/mk-fixture")
        echo "  mktemp calls in this script: $N_MK; of them a plain file: $N_MKF; the plain-file count on a fixture holding one: $N_MKC"
        check "this script makes one mktemp call, a directory, and no plain file (change 35)" "$(yn mk_counts_ok)"
        check "control: the plain-file count finds the one in a fixture (change 35)" "$(yn [ "$N_MKC" = 1 ])"
        echo "THIS MODE DOES NOT PUSH. The push (push mode, appended below) runs only"
        echo "on planning's word and the maintainer's authorisation typed in the"
        echo "implementing session (specs/0003-ci.md, the section on the push). The"
        echo "record is not split: this log, ci-run.log and scan.log go in one record"
        echo "commit after the push."
        echo
        self_shapes
        echo
        echo "## the generator and the generated scripts (change 21)"
        echo "command: sha256sum of <home>/.cache/emend-build/m7p1-close/gen.py and of the three scripts beside this one"
        echo "  gen.py:            $(sha256sum <"$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m7p1-close/gen.py" | cut -d' ' -f1)"
        for s in m7p1close-push.sh m7p1close-ci.sh m7p1close-scan.sh; do
          echo "  $s: $(sha256sum <"$(dirname "$0")/$s" | cut -d' ' -f1)"
        done
        echo "changes against M3 part 6's script (M4 part 1's close-out; the header above lists them in full; change 57):"
        echo "  19. the names, the spec, the base and the part 7 record check, M4 part 1's"
        echo "  20. REMOVED: the Excel-record check; in its place the count of records/excel-check-m2-*.md at HEAD, 0, with a control"
        echo "  21. HEAD's subject equals TIP_SUBJECT, with a control"
        echo "  22. CARGO_TARGET_DIR printed and checked to be <home>/.cache/emend-build/m4p1-close/target, with two controls"
        echo "changes against part 1's script (M4 part 2's close-out; the header above lists them in full):"
        echo "  23. the names, the spec, the base, TIP_SUBJECT and the part 1 record check, M4 part 2's"
        echo "  24. CARGO_TARGET_DIR checked to be <home>/.cache/emend-build/m4p2-close/target; the other-path control offers part 1's"
        echo "  25. change 20's block heading cites specs/0031 Out of scope"
        echo "  26. part 1's header item 22 reads ruling 2 where it read ruling 1 (specs/0030 close-out ruling 4)"
        echo "changes against M4 part 2's script (M5 part 1's close-out; the header above lists them in full):"
        echo "  28. the names, the spec, the base, TIP_SUBJECT and the M4 part 2 record check, M5 part 1's"
        echo "  29. CARGO_TARGET_DIR checked to be <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p1-close/target; the other-path control offers M4 part 2's; change 20's block heading cites specs/0032 Out of scope, its check label Milestones 4 and 5"
        echo "  30. the root line's <scratch> is the close-out's phase directory"
        echo "  31. TMPDIR set to <scratch>/tmp before mktemp, inherited by every tool run"
        echo "changes against M5 part 1's script (M5 part 2's close-out; the header above lists them in full):"
        echo "  33. the names, the spec, the base, TIP_SUBJECT and the M5 part 1 record check, M5 part 2's"
        echo "  34. CARGO_TARGET_DIR checked to be <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p2-close/target; the other-path control offers M5 part 1's; change 20's block heading cites specs/0033's opening paragraph"
        echo "  35. the TMPDIR input line, the under-TMPDIR check with its controls and the mktemp count (specs/0033 P1 ruling 12)"
        echo "  36. no Python call in this script, so nothing to change for -I -B"
        echo "changes against M5 part 2's script (M5 part 3's close-out; the header above lists them in full):"
        echo "  37. the names, the spec, the base, TIP_SUBJECT and the M5 part 2 record check, M5 part 3's"
        echo "  38. CARGO_TARGET_DIR checked to be <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p3-close/target; the other-path control offers M5 part 2's; change 20's block heading cites specs/0034's opening paragraph"
        echo "changes against M5 part 3's script (M5 part 4's close-out; the header above lists them in full):"
